{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966969,"nonce":"sURoAdGUb1teSGQ3IX/ukdBgXW0=","title":"Eight cn widgets still have no DSL binding","message":"52 of cn's widgets are reachable from `.blinc`. These eight are not, and\nthey are what is left of the family:\n\n| Widget | Lines | Shape it needs |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `DropdownMenu` | 1002 | Items as children, overlay anchored to a trigger. The overlay half exists; Popover, Tooltip and HoverCard all use the signal-as-handle watcher. |\n| `ContextMenu` | 955 | `DropdownMenu` opened by right-click rather than a trigger. |\n| `Menubar` | 1100 | A row of `DropdownMenu`s sharing which one is open. |\n| `NavigationMenu` | 823 | Menubar with panels rather than item lists. |\n| `Table` | 262 | Smallest file, but the only one that genuinely needs a list of structs: a row is not a scalar. |\n| `Tree` | 726 | Recursive children. Nothing else in the DSL nests a widget in itself yet. |\n| `Toast` | 519 | Queue plus timing, and a known exit-motion race on web. No trigger-shaped anchor, so it needs a host-side entry point. |\n| `Chart` | 1861 | The biggest surface in cn, and needs the list-of-structs type as much as `Table`. Last. |\n\nTry the children shape first — most are option lists, and only `Table`\nand `Chart` clearly need a row type.\n\nWhere a cn widget's state type has no DSL equivalent, add an accepting\nenum rather than narrowing at the call site. `Pagination` wanted\n`State\u003cusize\u003e`, which the DSL has no signal for, so `PageValue` takes\neither that or a `NumberValue` and rounds at the boundary. Converting\ninstead would have minted a second signal id and left the binding\nwriting to a copy.\n\nDetail lives in the \"In progress\" section of\n`crates/blinc_dsl_core/ROADMAP.md`.","files":null}]}